  1→# Shared Config Propagation Implementation Plan
  2→
  3→## Overview
  4→
  5→Implement shared configuration file propagation across Dual workspaces. When users define a `[shared]` section in `.dual.toml`, gitignored files (`.env`, `.vercel/`, etc.) are automatically managed via a central shared directory (`~/.dual/shared/{repo}/`). The main workspace symlinks to the shared dir; branch workspaces receive copies. Users run `dual sync` to refresh branch copies.
  6→
  7→## Current State Analysis
  8→
  9→- `.dual.toml` (`RepoHints`) supports `image`, `ports`, `setup`, `env` — no `[shared]` section
 10→- `cmd_add()` creates `.dual.toml` with defaults, registers workspace with `path: Some(...)`
 11→- `cmd_create()` registers branch workspace with `path: None`
 12→- `cmd_launch()` clones branch workspace via `git clone`, loads hints, creates container
 13→- No shared directory, no symlink infrastructure, no sync command exists
 14→- `WorkspaceEntry` has no parent/source reference between workspaces
 15→
 16→### Key Discoveries:
 17→- `RepoHints` ignores unknown TOML fields (serde default), so adding `[shared]` is backwards-compatible (`src/config.rs:242-251`)
 18→- `clone_workspace()` does pure `git clone` — gitignored files are lost (`src/clone.rs:27-74`)
 19→- Container creation only uses `hints.image` — `hints.env` is parsed but dropped (`src/main.rs:224-230`)
 20→- `detect_git_repo()` in `main.rs:511-545` can detect repo context from current directory
 21→- State directory structure: `~/.dual/` already exists for `workspaces.toml`
 22→
 23→## Desired End State
 24→
 25→1. `.dual.toml` supports a `[shared]` section listing files/directories to propagate
 26→2. `dual add` auto-moves listed files from main workspace to `~/.dual/shared/{repo}/`, creates symlinks back
 27→3. `dual launch` (branch) copies listed files from `~/.dual/shared/{repo}/` into the cloned workspace
 28→4. `dual sync` (in branch) re-copies from shared dir, refreshing stale files
 29→5. `dual sync` (in main) prompts for confirmation, then force-syncs ALL branch workspaces
 30→6. On Windows: copy instead of symlink everywhere (no symlinks at all)
 31→
 32→### Verification:
 33→- User adds repo with `[shared] files = [".vercel", ".env.local"]`
 34→- `.vercel/` and `.env.local` are moved to `~/.dual/shared/{repo}/`, symlinks created in main workspace
 35→- User creates and launches a branch → branch gets copies of `.vercel/` and `.env.local`
 36→- User runs `vercel pull` in main → updates flow through symlink to shared dir
 37→- User runs `dual sync` in branch → branch gets fresh copy of updated files
 38→- Changes in branch `.env.local` do NOT affect shared dir or other branches
 39→
 40→## What We're NOT Doing
 41→
 42→- No auto-detection of common file patterns (`.env*`, `.vercel/`) — users MUST define `[shared]`
 43→- No file watching daemon — sync is manual via `dual sync`
 44→- No Docker volume mount changes — shared files are in the workspace dir (visible to bind mount)
 45→- No `dual destroy` changes — shared dir persists independently of workspace lifecycle
 46→- No `[env]` wiring (separate concern, already documented in env-vars research)
 47→
 48→## Implementation Approach
 49→
 50→Three phases: (1) config schema + shared module, (2) CLI integration, (3) tests. The shared module is pure filesystem logic with no Docker or git dependencies, making it independently testable.
 51→
 52→---
 53→
 54→## Phase 1: Config Schema + Shared Module
 55→
 56→### Overview
 57→Add `[shared]` support to `RepoHints` and create `src/shared.rs` with all filesystem logic for managing the shared directory.
 58→
 59→### Changes Required:
 60→
 61→#### 1. Add `SharedConfig` to config
 62→**File**: `src/config.rs`
 63→**Changes**: Add `SharedConfig` struct and optional field on `RepoHints`
 64→
 65→```rust
 66→/// Shared configuration file propagation settings.
 67→#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq, Clone)]
 68→pub struct SharedConfig {
 69→    /// Files and directories to share across workspaces.
 70→    /// e.g. [".vercel", ".env.local", ".env"]
 71→    #[serde(default)]
 72→    pub files: Vec<String>,
 73→}
 74→```
 75→
 76→Add to `RepoHints`:
 77→```rust
 78→/// Shared files to propagate across workspaces
 79→#[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
 80→pub shared: Option<SharedConfig>,
 81→```
 82→
 83→Update `Default` impl to include `shared: None`.
 84→
 85→#### 2. Add `shared_dir` helper to config
 86→**File**: `src/config.rs`
 87→**Changes**: Add function to compute shared directory path
 88→
 89→```rust
 90→/// Get the shared config directory for a repo: ~/.dual/shared/{repo}/
 91→pub fn shared_dir(repo: &str) -> Option<PathBuf> {
 92→    dirs::home_dir().map(|home| home.join(".dual").join("shared").join(repo))
 93→}
 94→```
 95→
 96→#### 3. Create shared module
 97→**File**: `src/shared.rs` (new)
 98→**Changes**: Core logic for shared file management
 99→
100→```rust
101→use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
102→
103→/// Ensure the shared directory exists for a repo.
104→pub fn ensure_shared_dir(repo: &str) -> Result<PathBuf, SharedError> {
105→    let dir = crate::config::shared_dir(repo).ok_or(SharedError::NoHomeDir)?;
106→    std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).map_err(|e| SharedError::Filesystem(dir.clone(), e))?;
107→    Ok(dir)
108→}
109→
110→/// Initialize shared directory from the main workspace.
111→///
112→/// For each file in `files`:
113→/// - If file exists in workspace and is NOT already a symlink to shared dir:
114→///   move it to shared dir, create symlink back (Unix) or copy back (Windows)
115→/// - If file is already a symlink to shared dir: skip
116→/// - If file doesn't exist in workspace: skip
117→///
118→/// Returns list of files that were moved.
119→pub fn init_from_main(
120→    workspace_dir: &Path,
121→    shared_dir: &Path,
122→    files: &[String],
123→) -> Result<Vec<String>, SharedError>
124→
125→/// Copy shared files into a branch workspace.
126→///
127→/// For each file in `files`:
128→/// - If file exists in shared dir: copy to workspace (overwrite if exists)
129→/// - If file doesn't exist in shared dir: skip
130→///
131→/// Returns list of files that were copied.
132→pub fn copy_to_branch(
133→    workspace_dir: &Path,
134→    shared_dir: &Path,
135→    files: &[String],
136→) -> Result<Vec<String>, SharedError>
137→```
138→
139→**Key implementation details for `init_from_main`**:
140→
141→```rust
142→for file in files {
143→    let src = workspace_dir.join(file);
144→    let dst = shared_dir.join(file);
145→
146→    if !src.exists() {
147→        continue; // File not present yet, skip
148→    }
149→
150→    // Check if already a symlink pointing to shared dir
151→    if src.symlink_metadata().map(|m| m.is_symlink()).unwrap_or(false) {
152→        if let Ok(target) = std::fs::read_link(&src) {
153→            if target == dst {
154→                continue; // Already set up correctly
155→            }
156→        }
157→    }
158→
159→    // Ensure parent dir exists in shared
160→    if let Some(parent) = dst.parent() {
161→        std::fs::create_dir_all(parent)?;
162→    }
163→
164→    // Move file/dir to shared dir
165→    // Use copy + remove for cross-device moves (rename fails across filesystems)
166→    copy_recursive(&src, &dst)?;
167→    remove_recursive(&src)?;
168→
169→    // Create symlink back (Unix) or copy back (Windows)
170→    #[cfg(unix)]
171→    {
172→        std::os::unix::fs::symlink(&dst, &src)?;
173→    }
174→    #[cfg(windows)]
175→    {
176→        copy_recursive(&dst, &src)?;
177→    }
178→}
179→```
180→
181→**Helper functions** (private in `src/shared.rs`):
182→
183→```rust
184→/// Recursively copy a file or directory.
185→fn copy_recursive(src: &Path, dst: &Path) -> Result<(), SharedError>
186→
187→/// Remove a file or directory.
188→fn remove_recursive(src: &Path) -> Result<(), SharedError>
189→```
190→
191→`copy_recursive` logic:
192→- If `src` is a file: `std::fs::copy(src, dst)`
193→- If `src` is a directory: create dst dir, iterate entries, recurse
